{
  "source": "Phase-1 regression set (iter-13/iter-14 validation beats): full narrator response documents distilled from two live agent-in-the-loop sessions (session 1: seed 125, log logs/run_125_0.jsonl; session 2: seed 8, the theft-and-arson scenario, log logs/run_8_1.jsonl - gitignored runtime artifacts; provenance worklog iter-13/iter-14). Each case replays through the REAL mediator cycle (Simulator + Mediator + SceneLedger, cli/mediator.py) - not the validator or the gateway in isolation: the beat-level pins behind the phase-1 exit criterion '0 canon violations per 100 beats' (ROADMAP 2). After iter-14 the corpus pins every validator refusal reason at the beat level (incl. event_type_mismatch, cannot_know), the stale_ref gateway refusal, the full delta vocabulary (established/pinned/retired/no-op), the regen-exhaustion ladder, and both door outcomes (committed success + committed intent_rejected; rebased intents). The string 'anchor' in expected_event_seq / based_on_event_seq resolves to the anchor the emitted call advertised (the narrator's contract, BRIEF_SPEC 7.1); integers pass through. Expectations: status + note substrings (+ optional last_event_type, log_unchanged vs the emit moment, call_contains on a final emit).",
